Wine (ARM64EC build for aarch64)
================================

This is the Debian packaging of an ARM64EC-enabled wine for aarch64
hosts, converted from the Fedora `wine-git` RPM spec that used to live
in this repository. It builds:

  - wine           metapackage (core + common + desktop + fonts)
  - wine-core      loader, wineserver, builtin PE DLLs (aarch64-windows,
                   i386-windows, unix libs), wine.inf
  - wine-common    wrapper scripts (winecfg, wineboot, regedit, ...)
  - wine-desktop   desktop files, icons, binfmt.d handler, ntsync.conf
  - wine-fonts     wine fonts + fontconfig integration
  - wine-dev       widl, winebuild, winegcc, headers, import libraries

Differences from a stock Debian wine:

  * configured with --enable-archs=arm64ec,aarch64,i386 and
    --with-mingw=llvm-mingw (bylaws llvm-mingw toolchain provides the PE
    clang/lld 21; trixie's system lld 19 rejects winebuild's ARM64X
    .CRT section symbols), so 32-bit Windows code runs through FEX
    (package fex-emu-wine provides libwow64fex.dll / libarm64ecfex.dll)
  * wine-staging patchset applied, plus the bylaws ARM64EC rebase and
    the additional fixes listed in debian/changelog
  * d3d8/d3d9/d3d10/d3d10core/d3d11/dxgi/d3d12(d3d12core) are managed
    with update-alternatives, so wine-dxvk and wine-vkd3d-proton can
    take over per DLL (wine builtin = priority 10)
  * /usr/bin/wine and /usr/bin/wineserver are update-alternatives links
    pointing at the 64-bit binaries

The wine binfmt handler is registered via /usr/lib/binfmt.d/wine.conf;
systemd-binfmt picks it up after installation.

CJK font replacements (from the old wine-cjk patch) map SimSun/MS
Gothic/Batang and friends to WenQuanYi/VL Gothic/Nanum families; the
matching font packages are only Recommends of wine-fonts.

Prefix layout is the usual ~/.wine; see README-tahoma (shipped in
wine-fonts) for the tahoma bitmap configuration.
